</h3><div class="views-field views-field-created-1"><div class="field-content date-published">  <time datetime="2026-09-30T08:30:00-04:00">September 30, 2026</time>

 | News Release
</div></div><div><p class="blog-summary">Real gross domestic product (GDP) increased at an annual rate of 2.2 percent in the second quarter of 2026 (April, May, and June), according to the third estimate released today by the U.S. Bureau of Economic Analysis (BEA). In the first quarter, real GDP increased 2.5 percent (revised). The contributors to the increase in real GDP in the second quarter were consumer spending, investment, and exports. Imports, which are a subtraction in the…</p></div><div class="views-field views-field-title-1"><span class="field-content"><p><a href="  /news/2026/gdp-third-estimate-industries-corporate-profits-state-gdp-and-state-personal-income-2nd
