">U.S. International Transactions and Investment Position, 2nd Quarter 2026</a>
</h3><div class="views-field views-field-created-1"><div class="field-content date-published">  <time datetime="2026-09-24T08:30:00-04:00">September 24, 2026</time>

 | News Release
</div></div><div><p class="blog-summary">The U.S. current-account deficit resulting from international economic transactions widened by $33.4 billion, or 15.7 percent, to $246.0 billion in the second quarter of 2026, according to statistics released today by the U.S. Bureau of Economic Analysis. The revised first-quarter deficit was $212.6 billion. The second-quarter deficit was 3.0 percent of current-dollar gross domestic product, up from 2.7 percent in the first quarter.
</p></div><div class="views-field views-field-title-1"><span class="field-content"><p><a href="  /news/2026/us-international-transactions-and-investment-position-2nd-quarter-2026
">Read More&nbsp;<i class="fa fa-arrow-circle-right" aria-hidden="true"></i></a></p></span></div></div>
